Such figures aren't used.
"People have been knocked through doors and windows," says Pauli Sivonen from the Serlachius Museum.
Sivonen estimates that the number of visitors for the whole year in the Serlachius museums this year will approach one hundred thousand.
In previous years, there have been about 40 000 visitors.
Mänttä-Vilppula, located halfway between Tampere and Jyväskylä, has about 11 000 inhabitants.
Sivonen, Museum Director, reminds us that new museums are always phenomena when they open.
"The challenge is to make the phenomenon permanent," he says.
In Mänttä, it is hoped that the art season will continue well into the summer.
In the autumn, new exhibitions will be opened at the art museum.
