The Kainuu District Court will issue a verdict on the matter later.
In many places, August was exceptionally warm.
According to the Finnish Meteorological Institute, an equally warm August is repeated on average once every ten years.
The statistics of the Finnish Meteorological Institute show that the average temperature in the whole country was higher than usual.
In most parts of the country, the deviation was one to two degrees.
Due to the heat of July and August, the whole summer became warmer than usual.
The highest temperature of the whole summer was recorded in the first week of August in Pori, where the meter showed 32.8 degrees.
Lenny Henry says, “My father never hugged me.
He never said he loved me
Henry was born to a family of migrants from Jamaica in Dudley in the British Midlands region in 1958.
Henry's father worked at the factory and died when Henry was 19 years old. The relationship between the son and the father was distant.
Henry is currently rehearsing for Rudy’s Rare Records, a comedy show based partly on an imaginary conversation with his father, developed on the basis of a series of Radio 4 channels.
The soundtrack is a mixture of reggae and rapper in the upbeat pace.
Henry has had to go through painful childhood memories.
He's been in therapy many times since his mother died, and he reflects a lot on his relationship with his father.
It was very difficult to read my father.
His face was never seen, only the voice said: End the noise.
Just leave your sister alone.
Go! Move!
I'll look at cricket now.
My older brothers Seymour and Hilton, who were already adults when I was a child, went to the pub with my father and talked, for example, about the shape of a pint of beer or the beauty of a cricket punch.
I never talked to him about things like that.
For the most part of my life, he was for me the smileless man in the corner, reading his newspaper.
Henry recently opened a metal digestion in Dudley and thus got an idea of what his father's life must have been like, although the working conditions are better today than at that time.
Melters are a bit brighter today, but they are practically dark, smoky, labyrinth-like depths that plunge with flames, smoke and soot, which bring to mind the underworld.
Dad used to take a bath and just lie down in the tub, and he slowly began to sing to himself as he washed the dirt from the smeltery away from himself.
As I walked around the smeltery, I realized that he had been doing that job for years to get us food for the table, and I began to appreciate him more.
Nonetheless, Henry's childhood lacked the closeness offered by his parents.
My father never hugged and never said he loved me.
It wasn't until my mother started to get sick a little before she died that we started repeating to each other that we loved each other.
Henry has a Billie daughter with Dawn French, and through his own child he has been able to share the love he lacked as a child.
Do you have to keep repeating ‘I love you’?
Quit hugging already!
Dad, I'm 22!
It's with Dawn French.
Why don't we be friends?
She's an amazing mother
Henry is still a good friend with French, with whom she was married for 25 years.
Dawn's a good person.
Why don't Dawn and I be friends?
She's an amazing mother.
Henry's own mother had diabetes.
It was also one of the reasons that led to the mother's death.
As I began to suffer from a high level of overweight and diabetes symptoms, my doctor told me to make a complete turnaround.
After that, I started exercising a lot, and I also had to start a heavy diet to reduce symptoms.
It's very difficult –
and dull.
No one enjoys eating carrots.
Henry's well-knowned, short beard perhaps describes his change during his career development.
After receiving a lot of positive feedback from critics about his role as Othello, he is immersed in theatre.
Next up were Erhdysten's comedy and August Wilson's Fences.
Making theatre offers a different experience than sitcoms and comedies, which Henry has done throughout his busy career.
Henry started in the industry when he was only a 16-year-old factory worker.
A DJ spotted him on stage doing impersonations and contacted the New Faces talent show.
“For quite a long time, I was the only black imitator and comedian on TV,” he says.
Henrey learned while he was working.
I had to grain as an adult in the spotlight of publicity, I had to learn how to produce jokes from a conveyor belt between 1975 and 1985, while I lived stardom and was on television. It was a difficult time.
Lenny New Faces in 1975
Henry's manager had stage rights to The Black and White Minstrel Show, a light entertainment program in which the characters appeared in make-ups, so Henry ended up as a comedian on the show for five years.
My family didn't like it.
On the other hand, I wish I would never have taken part in it, but I don't regret it.
Even though my position was strange and objectionable, I got to work at huge events and learned how to deal with the audience.
Still, “British TV’s award-winning, multi-year favorite and light entertainment show” was “a grotesque parody of black people.”
In the 80's, Henry worked on another comedy series, where both pranks were made and admired for black British culture.
The first episode of The Lenny Henry Show was shown in 1984, and in the 90’s Henry was known for his character, chef Gareth Blacklock in the comedy series Chef!
That's the next decade Henry spent with commercials, documentaries, TV series, and movie parts, but after his LennyHenry.tv series on the BBC in 2008, he said to himself, ‘What are you going to do next, Len—now it looks like you’re just pedaling on your spot or you’re siding.”
Next up was Radio 4’s documentary series “What’s So Great About...?”.
In the first part we dealt with Shakespeare.
I've always tried to avoid Shakespeare.
It wasn't really taught to us at school, and I think it belonged to the white middle class, who wears stockings and has money.
That's what's why the Shakespeare topic aroused fear in me.
All the people we interviewed on the show – Peter Hall, Trevor Nunn, Adrian Lester, Judi Dench – said to me, “Try.
Don't forsake the whole thought until you know what you're talking about.
Date words and you'll understand why we all love Shakespeare so much.
Henry recited 20 verses of Othello's last speech for the documentary and he was sold.
I felt I could do this.
It almost felt as if some part of me had been missing before, and now it was put in place.
“That’s what it’s all about, it’s important, so take it seriously, learn your verses, do a little background research.
So the rehearsal process was tough, and I read the play for months before it was carried out.
In the end, the play was a success.
It was apparently expected to fail, but that didn't quite happen.
Shortly thereafter, Henry played the lead role in the Comedy of Mistakes.
All of a suddence, I acted in the British National Theatre, and I couldn't really believe it.
At one point, I thought, “Oh, you’ve changed.”
Once there were technical problems in the play, and Henry clearly felt that it was his job to entertain the audience.
‘A small voice in my mind said to me, ‘You have to manage for 10 minutes alone until the computer works again.”
On the other hand, the supervisor's assistant announced that the proposal would continue as soon as the problem has been fixed.
I walked off the stage, and a part of me breathed a sigh of relief.
It's not my responsibility,
I can leave it to others.
‘You’re a part of the play, stick to your role’
‘Fences’ at Duchess
Learninging lines for the ‘Fences’ play was challenging.
