01.09.2014 15:20 Retail chain Lidl seems to have got the Finns on their side, at least if there is faith in the result figures.
Lidl Suomi Kommandiittiyhtiö Group, which operates the trading group Lidl, continued to grow during the financial year that ended at the end of February.
The company also increased its earnings.
Earnings before taxes amounted to 79.6 million euros, compared with 56.4 million euros a year earlier.
Net sales, on the other hand, swelled from 960 million euros to 1.2 billion euros.
The increase was 25 per cent.
The company, which has increased its market shares, also improved its operating result from 61 million euros to 84 million euros.
The operating profit margin was 7.1.
Lidl's financial year lasts from the beginning of March to the end of February.
According to the company, the company paid 13.7 million euros in tax to Finland for the financial year that ended in February.
The company, which has continuously expanded its store chain, has announced that it will invest 100 million euros in Finland this year.
There are currently 142 Lidl stores in Finland and it employs more than 4 000 people.
The first stores were opened in 2002.
