Australian celebrities and Gabi Grecko in the nude photo scandal
Geoffrey Edelsten has declared himself outraged by hackers after his fiancé and nude photos of Hollywood's A-list star Gabi Grecko.
The entertainment world has been buzzing since Jennifer Lawrence's nudes were posted on the Internet as a result of an extensive celebrity image hacking scandal.
The hacker is said to have a total of 60 nudes of the Hunger Games star Lawrence and other superstars, such as supermodel Kate Upton and Cara Delevingne, singer Rihanna, Ariana Grande and Lea Michelle, and actress Kirsten Dunst.
Photographs of Australian actors Teresa Palmer, Emily Browning, Yvonne Strahovsky and Grecko, who lives in Melbourne, have also apparently been stolen in connection with the iCloud leak.
There are 101 celebrities on the list.
Edelsten, who proposed to Grecko last month, told Confidential, "this is disgusting."
All personal communication and images should remain private.
It is disgraceful that private information can be stolen and disseminated.
Greckon, based in New York, is reported to have commented on the case in an online magazine as ‘shameful’ and said the victims “feel disgusted.”
The hacker is believed to have 30 photos of Palmer with his previous boyfriend Scott Speedman, including two shots of Palmer topless on the edge of the basin.
Palmer's cinematic merits include "Love and Honor" with co-star Liam Hemsworth.
Palmer, Chuck star Strahovski and Sucker Punch actor Browning didn't comment on the hacked photos yesterday.
Lawrence's spokesman told TMZ magazine that "it's a brazen invasion of privacy."
Actor Seth Rogen was angered by the hacker in a tweet: ‘Publing stolen photos of a cell phone is in no way different from selling a stolen product.’
The publication of stolen images should not be made possible, just from a legal point of view.
Finland played almost as if on their home turf and rose to a sensational victory over Cuba in the volleyball World Cup.
See pictures of the fan fever.
Katowice of Poland was white on Monday: not Polish red-white, but Finnish blue-and-white.
According to STT, almost 2000 Finnish supporters followed Finland's victory at the Spodek arena.
It felt like I was playing at home.
That's how much of an impact the fans had on our game, Finland's captain Antti Siltala told STT.
Finland was already 0-2 in the game, but emerged 3-2.
In the fourth period, Finland made a miraculous ascension behind six points.
Cuba was already 16-10 in the period, but after that the Finns got the ecstasy on top.
However, a couple of hundred Finnish fans had to be disappointed when an on the field, the charter plane was unable to land in Katowice due to heavy fog.
The fans who ended up in Warsaw were late for the match.
Finnish football fans have beaten Europe at a rapid pace in recent days.
More than 8000 Finnish fans will be present at the World Basketball Championship in Bilbao, Spain.
It was as if every Finnish basket had been the victorial basket of the match, USA star Stephen Curry praised the Finnish basketball fans after Saturday's game.
The Council meeting will not be broadcast live due to technical problems
It is not possible to watch the Kouvola City Council's meeting live online today.
According to the city's announcement, the shipment is not possible due to technical problems.
The city of Kouvola regrets the situation.
You can watch the recording a few days after the meeting.
It has been possible to see the meetings of the Kouvola City Council via the internet since the beginning of the year.
For the next time, decision-making can be followed live on 13.10.2014.
The council's meeting videos can be found at http://www.kouvola.fi/index/aikuisvaestolle/paatoksenteko/valtuustoverkkossa.html and from the YouTube channel of the City of Kouvola.
